※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ `⎕empty` gives everything in an arena back at once, and every name holding something made
※ there is dead from that point: reading it would read memory the arena may already have
※ handed out again.  A name given something new is alive again.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let both: str = "a" ⧺ "b" in scratch
    ⎕empty(scratch)
    if both = "ab": 0u6 else: 1u6
